INFO:agents.coder_agent:Plan:
1. Define a Node class for singly linked list nodes with a value and a next pointer.
2. Define a LinkedList class with a head pointer initialized to None.
3. Implement insert(value) to add a new node at the beginning of the list.
4. Implement delete(value) to remove the first node with the given value, handling empty list and non-existent values.
5. Implement search(value) to return True if a node with the value exists, else False.
6. Implement reverse() to reverse the linked list in place.
7. Put all code in linked_list.py ensuring no use of built-in lists for core logic.
